    {
      "id": "TRIFECTA001",
      "title": "Cross-server lethal trifecta present (invisible to per-server scanners)",
      "severity": "critical",
      "message": "This fleet can simultaneously (1) read private data, (2) ingest untrusted content, and (3) communicate externally. The three capabilities are spread across different servers, so no single-server audit would catch this. An attacker only needs to plant instructions in any untrusted content the agent reads.",
      "location": "fetch+git",
      "evidence": [
        "private_data: git::git_diff_unstaged",
        "untrusted_content: fetch::fetch",
        "exfil: git::git_diff_staged, git::git_commit, git::git_log, git::git_show"
      ],
      "remediation": "Break the trifecta: remove or sandbox one leg. Common fixes: run untrusted-content tools in an isolated agent that has no private-data or exfil tools; require human approval on exfil actions; or apply content provenance / taint tracking so untrusted text can't trigger sensitive reads followed by outbound calls."
    },
    {
      "id": "TRIFECTA002",
      "title": "Example attack path #1",
      "severity": "high",
      "message": "Untrusted content enters via `fetch::fetch`, is used to read private data via `git::git_diff_unstaged`, and is exfiltrated via `git::git_diff_staged` (2 server(s) involved).",
      "location": "fetch->git->git",
      "evidence": [
        "entry:  fetch::fetch - Fetches a URL from the internet and optionally extracts its contents as markdown. Although originally you did not have i",
        "source: git::git_diff_unstaged - Shows changes in the working directory that are not yet staged",
        "sink:   git::git_diff_staged - Shows changes that are staged for commit"
      ],
      "remediation": ""
    },
    {
